# Project Rules

**Project:** Fibr - AI-Powered Twitter Content Generator  
**Purpose:** Fibr-specific rules for supreme coding agent performance.

---

## PROJECT ARCHITECTURE RULES

### Module System
- **IIFE pattern mandatory:** All modules wrapped in `(function() { ... })();`
- **Window exposure:** `window.ModuleName = ModuleName;` at end of module
- **Prototype augmentation:** Modules augment main class: `Object.assign(l.prototype, window.ModuleName);`
- **No ES6 modules:** Use IIFE. Maintain compatibility.

### File Organization
- **Core files:** `src/extension/background.js`, `content.js`, `popup.js`, `popup.html`
- **Modules:** `src/extension/modules/` - all feature code here
- **Shared:** `src/shared/` - reusable components
- **Build output:** `dist/extension/` - never edit directly
- **Edit source only:** Changes in `src/`. Build generates `dist/`.

### Build Process
- **Build command:** `npm run build:extension`
- **Watch mode:** `npm run dev:extension` for development
- **Reload required:** After build, reload extension in Chrome
- **No manual dist edits:** Build process manages dist/

---

## CODE PATTERNS

### Service Worker (`background.js`)
- **API calls only:** All Gemini API calls routed through background script
- **Retry logic:** Exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s max)
- **Rate limit handling:** Detect 429. Return `{ rateLimited: true, retryAfter: ms }`
- **Fallback model:** Try `gemini-1.5-flash` if `gemini-2.0-flash` fails
- **Error messages:** User-friendly. No technical jargon.

### Content Script (`content.js`)
- **IIFE wrapper:** Prevents redeclaration on multiple injections
- **Multi-strategy extraction:** 5 fallback strategies (site-specific → full body)
- **Sanitization pipeline:** DOM cleaning → text cleaning → AI preparation
- **Truncation:** 8000 char limit with intelligent cutoff at sentence boundary
- **Return format:** `{ success: boolean, content: string, error?: string }`

### Popup Logic (`popup.js`)
- **Class-based:** Main class instantiated after DOMContentLoaded
- **View system:** `showView(viewName)` - hide all, show target
- **Module loading:** Dynamic prototype augmentation after DOM ready
- **Defensive programming:** Null checks everywhere. Extension context invalidation handled.
- **Storage abstraction:** Use `getStorageItem/setStorageItem` methods. Not direct chrome.storage.

### Storage Operations
- **Keys:** `geminiApiKey`, `apiKeySet`, `hasSeenWelcome`, `theme`, `savedContent`, `chatHistory_${domain}`
- **Async/await:** All storage operations async. Handle errors.
- **Gallery limit:** 50 items max. Enforce in code.
- **Migration:** `savedThreads` → `savedContent`. Handle migration on init.

---

## API INTEGRATION RULES

### Gemini API
- **Endpoint:** `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/`
- **Model:** `gemini-2.0-flash:generateContent` (primary), `gemini-1.5-flash:generateContent` (fallback)
- **Rate limits:** 15 req/min, 1500/day (free tier)
- **Request format:** `{ contents: [{ role: 'user', parts: [{ text: prompt }] }] }`
- **Response parsing:** `response.data.candidates[0].content.parts[0].text`
- **Error handling:** Parse error JSON. Extract user-friendly message.

### Caching Strategy
- **Analysis cache:** 30-minute TTL (`twitter.js`). Reduce redundant API calls.
- **Validation cache:** 5-minute TTL (`validation.js`). Cache API key validation.
- **Cache keys:** Hash-based. Include content hash for analysis cache.
- **Cache invalidation:** Time-based. No manual clearing needed.

### Request Optimization
- **Request scheduler:** Prevent duplicate concurrent calls
- **Image prompts:** Manual only. Not automatic. Saves API quota.
- **Topic enhancer:** Disabled. Don't enable without quota analysis.
- **Batch operations:** Group related requests. Minimize API calls.

---

## CONTENT GENERATION RULES

### Tone System
- **Post tones (6):** Funny, Deeper Insights, Clever Observations, Industry Insights, Expert Repurpose, Content like this
- **Reply tones (5):** Fact Check, Amplify & Agree, Fact Check & Counter, Savage & Smart, Hypocrite Buster
- **Comment tones (2):** Praise, Ask
- **Custom mixing:** Allow combining any two tones. UI handles selection.

### Content Sanitization
- **Multi-layer:** DOM cleaning → text cleaning → AI preparation
- **Noise removal:** Scripts, ads, navigation, engagement metrics, timestamps
- **Twitter-specific:** Extract main tweet only. Not replies/timeline.
- **Site-specific:** News, blogs, docs, forums, ecommerce handled differently
- **Content limit:** 8000 chars max. Truncate intelligently.

### Character Counting
- **Unicode-aware:** Use `[...text].length` for grapheme-aware counting
- **Twitter limit:** 280 characters (Unicode-aware)
- **Generation range:** 50-2000 characters
- **Real-time updates:** Character counter updates on every keystroke

### Thread Generation
- **Page content threads:** From current webpage. Use page content.
- **Custom topic threads:** User-provided topic. Use AI knowledge base.
- **Three-step process:** Outline → Expand → Smart Split
- **Numbered cards:** Display as "1/8", "2/8", etc.
- **Auto-save:** Threads save to gallery automatically
- **Per-tweet prompts:** Optional image prompts per tweet

---

## UI/UX RULES

### Design System
- **Theme:** Glassmorphism with backdrop blur
- **Colors:** Black & white theme. Dark mode support.
- **Typography:** System fonts. No external fonts.
- **Size:** 400x600px popup default
- **Responsive:** Adapts to content. No fixed heights.

### Views
- **Welcome:** First-time onboarding
- **API Setup:** API key configuration
- **Chat:** Main content generation view
- **Gallery:** Saved content view (50 items max)
- **Settings:** Legacy API key management
- **Privacy:** Privacy policy view

### Navigation
- **View switching:** `showView(viewName)` - hide all, show target
- **Floating nav:** Bottom navigation bar (home, gallery)
- **Sidebar:** Hamburger menu (settings, gallery, privacy)
- **Back buttons:** Return to previous view

### User Feedback
- **Progress bars:** Show during API calls. `showProgressBar(message)`
- **Toast notifications:** Success/error messages. `showToast(message, duration)`
- **Loading states:** Spinners during operations
- **Status text:** Page status updates (`pageStatus.textContent`)

### Accessibility
- **ARIA labels:** All interactive elements labeled
- **Keyboard navigation:** Tab order logical
- **Screen readers:** Semantic HTML. Proper roles.
- **Focus management:** Focus moves appropriately on view changes

---

## ERROR HANDLING RULES

### Extension Context Invalidation
- **Common during dev:** Handle gracefully
- **Error message:** "Extension reloaded. Please refresh the page and try again."
- **Fallback:** Show welcome view. Don't crash.

### API Errors
- **429 Rate Limit:** Show friendly message. Don't retry immediately.
- **Network errors:** Retry with exponential backoff. Max 3 attempts.
- **Invalid API key:** Clear message. Don't leak key details.
- **Parse errors:** Handle malformed JSON. Provide fallback.

### Content Extraction Errors
- **Failed extraction:** Show error. Allow retry.
- **No content:** Check page type. Provide helpful message.
- **Protected pages:** Detect chrome:// pages. Show appropriate message.

### Storage Errors
- **Quota exceeded:** Handle gracefully. Clear old data if needed.
- **Permission denied:** Check manifest permissions. Provide fix guidance.

---

## PERFORMANCE RULES

### Code Optimization
- **Bundle size:** Minimize. Use esbuild minification.
- **Lazy loading:** Load modules on demand. Not all at once.
- **Virtual scrolling:** Gallery uses virtual scrolling for 50+ items
- **Debounce:** Search input debounced. Don't search on every keystroke.

### API Optimization
- **Cache analysis:** 30-minute TTL. Reuse cached analysis.
- **Batch requests:** Group related requests when possible
- **Request deduplication:** Prevent duplicate concurrent calls
- **Image prompts:** Manual only. Not automatic.

### Memory Management
- **Cleanup:** Remove event listeners on view changes
- **Limit gallery:** 50 items max. Enforce strictly.
- **Cache limits:** Don't cache indefinitely. TTL enforced.

---

## SECURITY RULES

### API Key Storage
- **Chrome Storage Local:** Encrypted by browser
- **Never log:** Don't log API keys. Don't expose in errors.
- **Validation:** Test API key before saving. Cache validation result.

### Content Security
- **XSS prevention:** Sanitize all user-generated content
- **CSP:** Content Security Policy enforced in manifest
- **No eval:** Never use eval or similar. No dynamic code execution.

### Input Validation
- **API keys:** Validate format. Check length. Test before save.
- **User input:** Sanitize all inputs. Validate before processing.
- **Content extraction:** Sanitize extracted content. Remove scripts.

---

## TESTING RULES

### Test Files
- **Location:** `tests/` directory
- **Runner:** `tests/run-all.js`
- **Coverage:** Twitter helpers, structured helpers, navigation helpers

### Test Requirements
- **New features:** Include tests with implementation
- **Edge cases:** Test boundaries. Invalid inputs.
- **Integration:** Test components together. Not isolated.

### Missing Tests
- **Content sanitization:** Needs comprehensive tests
- **API retry logic:** Needs retry scenario tests
- **Character counting:** Needs Unicode edge case tests

---

## MAINTENANCE RULES

### Code Quality
- **No legacy naming:** Replace "TabTalkAI" references with "Fibr"
- **Remove unused code:** Delete disabled features completely
- **Extract constants:** Move magic numbers to constants.js
- **Split large files:** twitter.js (3,014 lines) needs splitting

### Refactoring
- **Clear goal:** Know why refactoring. Execute precisely.
- **Test after:** Verify refactoring doesn't break functionality
- **Pattern consistency:** Follow established patterns. Don't introduce new ones.

### Documentation
- **Update MasterMemory:** Keep MasterMemory.md current
- **Code comments:** Explain why, not what
- **API docs:** Document function signatures. Parameters. Returns.

---

