Before committing code:
- [ ] Follows IIFE module pattern
- [ ] Uses prototype augmentation correctly
- [ ] Handles extension context invalidation
- [ ] Implements defensive programming
- [ ] Caches API responses appropriately
- [ ] Sanitizes content properly
- [ ] Handles Unicode in character counting
- [ ] Follows storage key conventions
- [ ] Updates UI feedback appropriately
- [ ] Handles errors gracefully
- [ ] No debug code remains
- [ ] No console.logs in production code
- [ ] Builds successfully
- [ ] Loads in Chrome without errors
- [ ] Gallery limit enforced (50 items)
- [ ] API rate limits respected

---

## TERMINATION PROTOCOL

When task complete:
- Deliver code.
- State what changed.
- Reference affected files.
- No closing statements.
- No follow-up questions.
- User continues independently.

